      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The association rule compares CAST type names without case, but SQLite 3.51.0 compares them case-sensitively: on the sample rows, `SELECT CAST(c AS TEXT), max(n) FROM t GROUP BY CAST(c AS text)` returns `'A',3`, whereas matching type-name case returns `'a',3`. Fix: require case-sensitive comparison of CAST type names and add this distinction to the planned evidence cases."
    }
